The Tale of Genji chapters 2–53 are in 1–1 correspondence with the 52 partitions of a 5-element set (the Bell number B_5), each partition recording which of five incense sticks share the same scent.  The sticks are canonically numbered left-to-right {1,2,3,4,5}; two sticks belong to the same block of the partition precisely when they are joined by a horizontal tie in the traditional Genji-kō diagram for that chapter.  

Chapter 39 (“Yūgiri”) is universally depicted with ties joining sticks 1–2 and sticks 4–5 while leaving stick 3 isolated, yielding the partition {{1,2},{3},{4,5}}.  (The same diagram is reproduced, for example, in the standard wood-block and modern typographic editions of the Genji-kō charts.)  The blocks are written in increasing order of their minimal elements, matching the format requested by the query.

